<p>ChatGPT now supports connecting multiple Google accounts for Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Contacts in supported accounts. OpenAI announced the change on August 28, 2026, making it possible to bring personal and work accounts into the same conversation. citeturn418603search12turn206364search1</p>
<h2>Can ChatGPT use more than one Google account?</h2><p>Yes, where the specific Google app supports multiple connected accounts on your account and surface. OpenAI's current guidance says some apps support more than one connected account and let you choose another account from Settings when the option is available. citeturn206364search1</p>
<h2>How do you connect a second Google account?</h2><ol><li>Open ChatGPT Settings and go to Apps or Plugins, depending on the interface.</li><li>Open the relevant Google app or connection.</li><li>Choose Connect another account when that option appears.</li><li>Sign in to the second Google account and review the requested permissions.</li><li>Finish Google's authorization flow and return to ChatGPT.</li></ol><p>OpenAI notes that availability depends on the app, plan, region, workspace and interface. citeturn206364search1</p>
<h2>Which Google services can you use together?</h2><p>The August 28 release note specifically names Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Contacts plugins. Google Drive has its own connection flow and can also be used with a connected Google account for files the account can access. citeturn418603search12turn803812search0</p>
<h2>Can ChatGPT mix personal and work accounts?</h2><p>It can, where the supported app and workspace rules allow it. The important point is permissions: connecting an account does not bypass that account's existing access. A work account cannot expose documents or email the user cannot already open. citeturn803812search0turn206364search1</p>
<h2>How do you avoid using the wrong Google account?</h2><p>Review the connected accounts before asking for data, and be specific in your request when multiple accounts are available. OpenAI says you can review connected accounts, reconnect an account, or disconnect an account from the app settings. citeturn206364search1</p>
<h2>What happens to permissions when you disconnect an account?</h2><p>Disconnecting stops future access through that account. It does not automatically delete existing conversations or saved data, so treat connection management and data retention as separate settings. citeturn206364search1</p>
<h2>What is the best setup for work and personal use?</h2><p>Keep the account purpose clear. A useful pattern is to connect your work Google account for project mail and calendars, your personal account for personal planning, and then name the account explicitly when a task could pull from both. Review permissions before adding a new connection.</p>
<h2>What about Google Drive?</h2><p>Google Drive connections work with the files and folders the chosen Google account can already access. OpenAI says personal and individual accounts have live access rather than administrator-managed sync, while managed workspaces can have additional admin controls. citeturn803812search0</p>
